!script {{
  --/| ==========================================================================
  --/| Tutorial 18: Discovering Dynamic D&D 2024 Beacon Features and Effects
  --/|
  --/| PURPOSE
  --/| Some Beacon record families cannot be documented as one fixed list of names.
  --/| Features and Effects depend on the character's classes, species, feats,
  --/| spells, items, and other content.
  --/|
  --/| A Feature called "Jack of All Trades," for example, does not guarantee that
  --/| every compatibility property related to it will use the full display name.
  --/| Observed compatibility names include jack, jack_attr, jack_bonus, and
  --/| jack_of_all_trades. Those names cannot be predicted from the Feature name.
  --/|
  --/| The reliable approach is to discover the canonical Feature or Effect records
  --/| that actually exist on the selected character and inspect their mapped leaves.
  --/|
  --/| SELECTORS
  --/| Numeric indexes are useful for discovery only. For reusable scripts, prefer
  --/| a unique record name or shortID after the probe has shown it to you.
  --/|
  --/| FEATURE RECORDS
  --/| Feature instances are dynamic. The reusable Feature schema includes name,
  --/| shortID, description, _enabled, arrayPosition, parentID, childIDs, relations.
  --/|
  --/| childIDs and relations are structural. A Feature's actual mechanics can live
  --/| in linked Roll Bonus, Resource, Action, Defense, Speed, Effect, Healing,
  --/| Spellcasting, or other canonical records.
  --/|
  --/| EFFECT RECORDS
  --/| Effects are also dynamic content. The currently mapped generic fields include
  --/| _id, type, name, recordName, shortID, _enabled, _active, description,
  --/| category, damageType, label, source, compendiumPageID, createdTime, parentID,
  --/| and childIDs.
  --/|
  --/| Effect _active can be read, and both true and false have been observed, but
  --/| Effect creation/removal/toggle lifecycle is NOT documented as a universal
  --/| safe ScriptCards write operation. This tutorial only reads Effects.
  --/|
  --/| This tutorial can produce a long card on feature-heavy characters. That is
  --/| intentional: it is a discovery tutorial, not a compact character sheet.
  --/| ==========================================================================

  --#beaconsheet|1
  --#sourcetoken|@{selected|token_id}
  --#title|[*S:character_name] - Dynamic Features and Effects Tutorial

  --+|[c][b]Feature Records[/b][/c]

  --%FeatureIndex|0;99;1
    --&FeatureName|[*S:features->[&FeatureIndex]->name]
    --?"[&FeatureName]" -eq "undefined"|%!

    --+|[b]Feature [&FeatureIndex]: [&FeatureName][/b]
    --+shortID|[*S:features->[&FeatureIndex]->shortID]
    --+description|[*S:features->[&FeatureIndex]->description]
    --+_enabled|[*S:features->[&FeatureIndex]->_enabled]
    --+arrayPosition|[*S:features->[&FeatureIndex]->arrayPosition]
    --+parentID|[*S:features->[&FeatureIndex]->parentID]
    --+childIDs|[*S:features->[&FeatureIndex]->childIDs]
    --+relations|[*S:features->[&FeatureIndex]->relations]
  --%|

  --+|[c][b]Effect Records[/b][/c]

  --%EffectIndex|0;99;1
    --&EffectName|[*S:effects->[&EffectIndex]->name]
    --?"[&EffectName]" -eq "undefined"|%!

    --+|[b]Effect [&EffectIndex]: [&EffectName][/b]
    --+_id|[*S:effects->[&EffectIndex]->_id]
    --+type|[*S:effects->[&EffectIndex]->type]
    --+recordName|[*S:effects->[&EffectIndex]->recordName]
    --+shortID|[*S:effects->[&EffectIndex]->shortID]
    --+_enabled|[*S:effects->[&EffectIndex]->_enabled]
    --+_active|[*S:effects->[&EffectIndex]->_active]
    --+description|[*S:effects->[&EffectIndex]->description]
    --+category|[*S:effects->[&EffectIndex]->category]
    --+damageType|[*S:effects->[&EffectIndex]->damageType]
    --+label|[*S:effects->[&EffectIndex]->label]
    --+source|[*S:effects->[&EffectIndex]->source]
    --+compendiumPageID|[*S:effects->[&EffectIndex]->compendiumPageID]
    --+createdTime|[*S:effects->[&EffectIndex]->createdTime]
    --+parentID|[*S:effects->[&EffectIndex]->parentID]
    --+childIDs|[*S:effects->[&EffectIndex]->childIDs]
  --%|

  --+|[c][b]What to Remember[/b][/c]

  --+Dynamic Names|Feature and Effect names come from character content, so there is no universal selector list.
  --+Discovery|Use a numeric index to discover records, then prefer a unique name or shortID in reusable scripts.
  --+Feature Mechanics|Follow childIDs and relations into the linked typed record families.
  --+Effect Safety|Read _active freely for diagnosis; do not assume Effect lifecycle writes are universally safe or verified.
}}
